meone else take the blame to protect her reputation.', 'character_utility': 'utility(Clara):\n\tProve my strategic brilliance in every scenario, particularly by winning games and tournaments, as this reinforces my self-worth and competence.\n\tEnsure that the team performs at its peak capacity, even if it means taking control or overriding inefficient ideas.\n\tEarn the respect and recognition of the group without appearing weak or vulnerable to others.\n\tOvercome the lingering belief that dependence on others is inherently risky, by learning to trust capable teammates.\n\tBalance my competitive drive with the ability to maintain positive relationships within the group, though this requires stepping out of my comfort zone.\n\tRefine my strategies and adapt to unexpected challenges during gameplay, demonstrating my quick-thinking proficiency.\n\tAvoid situations where I appear at fault or lose credibility, as maintaining my reputation is vital to my identity.\n\tPush through emotional barriers, even if gradually, to connect with others in a way that fosters both cooperation and mutual respect.', 'summarized_profile': 'Clara Matthews is a highly intelligent and competitive 24-year-old marketing intern who thrives on strategic challenges, particularly in her beloved world of board games. Behind her sharp mind and determination lies a guarded individual shaped by past humiliation, leaving her fearful of relying on others. Her laser-focus on winning often leads to isolation, as her dismissive attitude and obsession with control push others away. Though outwardly composed, Clara struggles with emotional connection and hides her personal passion by privately writing game strategy guides. Beneath her cold exterior lies a conflicted young woman yearning to balance ambition with meaningful relationships.'}, {'name': 'Eugene', 'role': 'side', 'profile': 'Name: Eugene Whittaker  \nGender: Male  \nAge: 58  \nOccupation: Retired history teacher  \n\nPrimary Strengths:  \n- Experienced and knowledgeable about traditional board games and strategies, often bringing a historical perspective to gameplay.  \n- Warm and nostalgic, creating an air of wisdom and mentorship for the group.  \n- Deeply values camaraderie and the original intent of group activities over competition.  \n\nPrimary Flaws:  \n- Resistant to change, dismissing modern strategies and innovations as frivolous or disrespecting the "true" spirit of board gaming.  \n- Struggles with feelings of irrelevance and insecurity when others excel using methods he doesn\'t understand or appreciate.  \n- Can become overly sentimental, clouding his judgment when faced with the need for adaptation.  \n\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior:  \n- Often interjects anecdotes or trivia about the history of specific games or strategies, whether or not it\'s relevant or wanted.  \n- Attempts to mediate arguments through appeals to tradition or shared values, but can inadvertently alienate those who prioritize modern approaches.  \n- Occasionally zones out into nostalgic reveries, appearing detached from the present moment.  \n\nPast Traumatic Event:  \n- Eugene once mentored a high school club that dissolved after a rift between members, which he blamed himself for failing to prevent. The experience left him deeply afraid of watching another group fall apart due to conflict or changing dynamics.  \n\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits:  \n1. Eugene might loudly berate the group for "ruining" the club\'s spirit, accusing them of prioritizing winning over fellowship.  \n2. He could abruptly leave a session, slamming the door as a symbolic protest against the group’s modern playstyles.  \n3. In heated moments, Eugene might dismiss Damon or others as "too inexperienced" to understand the real purpose of the club.  \n\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:  \n1. Eugene